# Enforce CSRF for cookie-authenticated DataFn writes

## Affected sites
- `services/account/src/app.ts:135` — passes the authenticate-only AuthFn provider to DataFn.
- `services/account/src/datafn/server.ts:103` — authenticates every DataFn action without distinguishing reads from writes.
- `services/account/src/datafn/server.ts:75` — public-link owner routes also use authenticate-only session resolution.
- `services/account/src/app.ts:177` — disallowed origins are rejected only for preflight; direct simple requests continue to route handlers.

## Required outcome
- Cookie-authenticated DataFn mutations, transactions, sync writes, and public-link owner operations validate the AuthFn CSRF token before execution, while bearer and API-key authentication continue to work without browser CSRF semantics.
- A direct state-changing request from a disallowed origin cannot commit data, regardless of whether the browser issues a preflight.
