**Close the databases even if the HTTP server fails to close.**

`closeServer` rejects when `serverInstance.close` reports an error, for example `ERR_SERVER_NOT_RUNNING`. The rejection propagates out of `shutdown`, so `services.close()`, `syncDatabase?.close()`, and `database.close()` never run and `process.exit(0)` never runs. The process then stays alive on SIGTERM with open Postgres pools until the orchestrator sends SIGKILL, and `void shutdown()` produces an unhandled rejection.

`services/account/src/worker.ts` already uses nested `finally` blocks for the same cleanup chain. Apply the same guarantee here.




<details>
<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-  await closeServer(server);
-  await services.close();
-  await syncDatabase?.close();
-  await database.close();
-  process.exit(0);
+  try {
+    await closeServer(server);
+  } catch (error) {
+    logger.error("nucleus account server close failed", { error });
+  }
+  try {
+    await services.close();
+  } finally {
+    try {
+      await syncDatabase?.close();
+    } finally {
+      await database.close();
+    }
+  }
+  process.exit(0);
```
</details>

