          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/569#discussion_r3888677730",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Derive cookie security from the supplied deployment regions**\n\nWhen callers supply HTTPS `deployment.regions` without setting a matching process-wide `ACCOUNT_AUTHORITY`, the declaration is initialized from `resolveRegions()` and its HTTP fallback rather than the supplied regions, making `secure` false for cookies issued on those HTTPS authorities. The previous implementation derived this value from the input region; build or configure the AuthFn declaration using the active deployment's default region so programmatically composed HTTPS services retain Secure cookies."
