          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Migrate region records before replacing the lookup adapter**\n\nOn existing dev/pre/live Cloudflare namespaces, this replacement cannot read the records written by `createCloudflareRegionLookupStore`: the old adapter stored each identifier in a hashed Durable Object under the `record` key, while the generic adapter targets one `nucleus_account:superfunctions-stores` object using `kv:` keys. Because the deployment reuses the existing `AuthFnRegionLookupDurableObject` migration without copying those records, region resolution starts missing established users once cached results expire, potentially routing them to a region where their account is absent; preserve a legacy reader or migrate the records during rollout.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L82-L85](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/d2988ed92c0b6c27e1912f17fb41e2213a9e19eb/AGENTS.md#L82-L85)"
