          "line": 17,
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/569#discussion_r3888887134",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Apply the DataFn schema before deploying sync workers**\n\nFor a fresh regional sync database, this local-only push command is the sole repository path that creates the generated DataFn tables: `.github/workflows/account-service-deploy.yml` invokes `scripts/deploy.mjs`, which only builds and deploys Workers, and no committed remote migration is applied. The new live Hyperdrive setup therefore permits a successful Worker deployment whose first `/datafn/*` database operation fails because tables such as `__datafn_changes` and the resource tables do not exist; add a versioned remote migration step before rolling out each sync binding.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L84-L85](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/d2988ed92c0b6c27e1912f17fb41e2213a9e19eb/AGENTS.md#L84-L85)"
