          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/569#discussion_r3889153607",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Migrate DynamoDB lookup records before switching adapters**\n\nThe existing Cloudflare migration concern has a second backend-specific instance when `AUTHFN_REGION_LOOKUP_TABLE` points to a populated DynamoDB table: the old adapter stored rows at `PK=<identifier>, SK=LOOKUP`, while AuthFn 0.2 requests `authfn:region:<identifier>` through this generic adapter, which stores it at `PK=KV#authfn:region:<identifier>, SK=KV`. Neither its current-key nor legacy-key lookup can read the old raw partition key, so established users lose their region placement after this switch; add a legacy DynamoDB reader or migrate those records before rollout.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L84-L85](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/97ed66977c68bf98a40b607d3c94e8877ffec712/AGENTS.md#L84-L85)"
