      "body": "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> No new issues were introduced by this follow-up, but existing must-address Pullfrog feedback remains open, so this review does not approve the PR.\n\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `d2988ed`, covering the account hardening follow-up and its interaction with the complete PR diff.\n\n- **Validated runtime numbers** — Consolidated positive and non-negative environment parsing for DataFn payload, rate-limit, and OpenSearch timeout/retry settings.\n- **Required verified database TLS** — Rejected insecure direct remote Postgres connection strings while preserving loopback development and Hyperdrive connections.\n- **Hardened diagnostics and shutdown** — Restricted production debug-sink delivery to HTTPS and made Node cleanup continue through HTTP server, service, sync database, and account database failures.\n- **Tightened composition contracts** — Consolidated shared type imports and exposed the test harness's concrete in-memory region lookup store without an unsafe cast.\n\n\n\n\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix it ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/nucleum/569?action=fix&review_id=5060587993) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/actions/runs/33307350227/job/99246121745) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>"
